    233          /**
    234           *  @brief      PI Regulator without anti-windup
    235           *  @details    PI controller algorithm.
    236           *              Definitions:
    237           *
    238           *              <b>e(t)</b> - input error in continuous time domain.
    239           *
    240           *              <b>u(t)</b> - controller output in continuous time domain.
    241           *
    242           *              <b>e(k)</b> - input error at step k - discrete time domain.
    243           *
    244           *              <b>u(k)</b> - controller output at step k - discrete time domain.
    245           *
    246           *              <b>e_max</b> - max range of e(k).
    247           *
    248           *              <b>u_max</b> - max range of u(k).
    249           *
    250           *            PI controller algorithm in <b>continuous time domain</b>:
    251           *
    252           *          \f[ u(t) = K\left(e(t) +\frac{1}{T_i}\int_0^t \! e(t) \, \mathrm{d}t. \right)\f]
    253           *           where:
    254           *            K :  controller gain
    255           *
    256           *            Ti: integral time constant
    257           *
    258           *           PI controller algorithm in <b>fractional arithmetic</b>:
    259           *
    260           *           \f[
    261           *             \begin{aligned}
    262           *                & u_f(k) = K_{p_{sc}} \cdot e_f(k) + u_f(k - 1) + K_{i_{sc}} \cdot e_f(k) \\
    263           *                & e_f(k) = \frac{e(k)}{e_{max}}\\
    264           *                & u_f(k) = \frac{u(k)}{u_{max}}\\
    265           *                & K_{p_{sc}} =  K \frac{e(k)}{e_{max}}\\
    266           *                & K_{i_{sc}} =  K \frac{T}{T_i}\frac{e(k)}{e_{max}}\\
    267           *             \end{aligned}
    268           *           \f]
    269           *           where:
    270           *           <b>T</b> : sampling time
    271           *
    272           *
    273           *  It stops integration when the sum of proportional and integral components exceeds the output limits
    274           *  and the two components have the same sign.
    275           *
    276           *  @param[in]      pi_params       = PI parameters: gains and limits
    277           *  @param[in]      err             = PI input error in Q17.15 notation
    278           *  @param[in, out] integ_term_k_1  = PI state variable in Q2.30 notation
    279           *  @return         PI output after saturation in Q2.30 notation
    280           */

