    462          /**
    463           *  @brief     Integral routine: it approximates the integral of an input quantities according to Backward-Euler Method.
    464           *  @details
    465           *  This function approximates the integral of an input signal according to the Backward-Euler Method.
    466           *  The output is not saturated, so overflow may occur.
    467           *
    468           *          Integrator in <b>continuous time domain</b>:
    469           *          \f[ y(t) =  K_i\int_0^t \! x(t) \, \mathrm{d}t. \f]
